=== READING
  If worstStateChangeNoRecentre is ORDERS below worstStateChange, the saturation is
  the frame translation and clause (a) should use the no-recentre quantity.
  If the two are COMPARABLE, the translation is not the cause and the saturation is
  in the physics or in the step itself -- which would need its own investigation
  before any convergence criterion can rest on a per-step change at all.
  And if the CONVERGED and TRANSIENT levels do not separate on the no-recentre
  quantity either, clause (a) cannot be made to work and (b)+(c) must carry it.

